fix(pip): Full review pass - variable power lens FOV, thermal facts, hygiene

Applied after reading both mods' sources instead of guessing. They share byte identical reticle
shaders; the only difference is one binding, so the engine contract is small and exact.

Variable power sights: the packs give the lens FOV at the two ends of the range
(scope_lense_fov at the highest power, scope_lense_fov_base at the lowest) plus
scope_dynamic_zoom, and the engine's stock ADS FOV is precisely the value between those ends
that the selected power asks for. The lens FOV now takes that value clamped into the declared
range, so the lens tracks the sight instead of sitting at one end. Both pack spellings
(scope_lens_fov and scope_lense_fov) are read; a sight whose config carries only the 3DSS
spelling previously fell through to GetSecondVPZoomFactor(), i.e. to no magnification at all.

Hygiene and latent items found by reviewing the whole change set rather than one file at a
time: the image dumps now require r__svp_debug 2 so a normal session never writes tens of
megabytes to disk, the dead s_lastMagTarget is gone, three stale comments that still described
the old alternating frame scheme are corrected, MT_PIP_BUILD is bumped, the upscaler post
process refuses to run for the second set (it owns frame level state), the $user$viewport2
remap exception carries the reason and the failure mode it would cause if removed, and the
Thermal facts are read from both sections that can carry them.